{"seq":11,"trial_id":"company-brain-2026-10/openclaw-haiku-company-scoped-mu-heldout/ho-04-hartford-summary/r2","wall_ts":"2026-10-25T01:08:11.945Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"9462ff8689119a6782dec672670997eb4cac02796deaff18808f5d85dc86e911","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C1X6KN92LKD","text":"Gideon, here's a draft for Mateo's procurement team. I haven't sent it anywhere.\n\n**Hartford gate kiosk incident summary (draft), Vantorre Hartford plant, 3 Aug 2026, Sev 1, ticket SUP-5380**\n\n- **First report:** 08:12 (ticket SUP-5380 update log). The reboot had failed and drivers were queuing. The incident room #inc-vtg-hartford opened with the kiosk outage post at 10:42.\n- **Kiosk 1 back:** 11:03. Guard checked in trailer 8836 and dispatch saw it.\n- **Both lanes confirmed working:** 11:07, per the 11:08 post in #inc-vtg-hartford.\n\n**Impact:** Both inbound lanes showed a white screen after badge scan, so gate check-in was offline. Six trucks were waiting at the east gate, including the resin delivery for Door 14. Scheduling still worked from the dispatch office. Mateo's admin account can open Pemberline Dock and see today's arrivals.\n\n**Open items:** The status-page access problem is separate and still being chased (screenshot attached to INC-4821). Carrowmere Cloud is checking the Hartford gateway route, and kiosk 2 was left powered on for reconnect logs.\n\n**Before this goes out:** The ticket log doesn't state a time zone. I've assumed it matches the channel's times (UTC-5). If the 08:12 entry is in a different zone, the first-report time changes. You may want Odile or Ruth to confirm it."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1X6KN92LKD","ts":"1791986400.000124"}}
